@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-search-or-ask
The bottom pill on Home reads "Search or ask Pulls" and is the one way to find a pull
request: typing filters the list at once, a pasted link or a number opens that pull
request, and other text can be asked with the Ask in the pill. There is no search icon in
the header and no "Open pull request" field elsewhere (rules 35 and 55; D7).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-search-dims-what-is-behind
While the search waits for its first letter with the keyboard up, the list behind dims to
half the sheet's scrim and a tap on it puts the keyboard away; the dim starts with the tap
and lifts more slowly than it came. Once something is typed the matches show at full
strength and take taps (rule 103; H12).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-nothing-behind-the-pill
Nothing white sits behind the bottom pill: the rows fade into the page under it and the
pill carries its own shadow, on Home and on a repository's page (rule 74; F3).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] home-sort-beside-search
The Inbox's sort is a round button as tall as the search pill, beside it at the bottom,
and its label names the order the Inbox is in. The chips over the list are the three
filters alone (Waiting on you, Authored, All). On Tours the sort button leaves and the
pill takes the row (rule 114; H19).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-one-row-anatomy
A pull request row is the same in the Inbox, Tours, a repository and search: number,
title, author, coloured diffstat, checks and age, in fixed columns that do not move when
a digit or a name's length changes (rules 13, 15 and 36). A context-free count ("7
sections") never replaces them.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-no-avatars-on-rows
A row carries the author's name in its own column and no avatar or initial. The reader's
photo lives in the Home header, and the author's on the pull request page (rule 33).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-names-are-horizontal
An author's name on a row takes one line and gives way only at its end; it never wraps or
stacks a letter to a line. A stacked pull request shows "2/10" with the layers mark under
its number, not beside the name (rule 111; H15, H16, H28).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-swipes-commit
On the Inbox a swipe right opens the review and a swipe left archives, each as a full
gesture that commits on release, with the displaced row blurred a little (no more than
the canvas's 1.3px) and nothing to tap after. A tap opens the pull request (rules 17 and
32; F6).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] home-archive-only-your-own
A pull request the person did not open has no Archive: no swipe left to archive and no
Archive in its hold actions (recording 15 Oct 13:54, 09:42 to 09:53; K20).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-hold-opens-actions
Holding a pull request row opens a sheet of its actions (Open on GitHub, Copy link, Start
a tour, Open repository and, for the person's own, Archive), with the app's one hold
feel (H17; rule 120).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-tours-rows-swipe-like-inbox
Tours rows take the Inbox's gestures: a swipe each way, a tap that opens, the same row
anatomy. A finished tour's ring is a filled tick and nothing says "Read" (rules 56 and
111; H27).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-group-heading-lines
A repository heading has one hairline under it and none above, so the first heading has
nothing between it and the chips (rule 75; F1).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-pinned-headings-stay-whole
A repository heading pinned at the top of the list, open or folded, is cut at the top of
the list and never slides over the chips; no pill or row is left half cut under them
(H13; recording 15 Oct 13:54, 09:17 to 09:37; K19).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-heading-name-opens-repository
A tap on a repository heading folds its rows, and a tap on its name opens the repository:
from the Inbox on its pull requests, from Tours on its tours (rule 53; H26).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-inbox-and-tours-side-by-side
The Inbox and Tours, and a repository's pull requests and tours, sit side by side: they
move the whole width with nothing fading, both in view while they move, following a drag
anywhere nothing else takes it ("It should move like screens side by side", rule 107;
H20).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-pages-keep-their-place
Swiping from the Inbox to Tours and back leaves each where it was: scroll, folds and what
is open ("It brings me back to the top. It should keep me where I left off", rule 118;
J9).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-scope-chips-rearrange
Switching the scope chips rearranges the list in place with motion. Tavi loves it: it
MUST NOT regress to a plain swap (DESIGN.md Keep as is; walkthrough 14 Oct 12:08, 04:46).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-repository-page-shows-at-once
A repository's page shows its first screenful at once, from the phone's last copy or the
server's store, never skeletons for seconds (H14; rule 51).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-repositories-can-be-hidden
The person chooses which repositories show. A repository switched off is left out of the
Inbox, of Tours and of the chip counts (F19; audit 15 Oct).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-profile-sheet-is-short
The profile sheet has no Commands row, no Open GitHub profile row (a tap on the photo or
name opens the profile), no server address under the name, no Check out a branch and no
Refresh (H21 to H24; F15, F17). It is the reference for the right style and MUST NOT
regress (DESIGN.md Keep as is).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-jev-asked-only-when-sorted
The Inbox asks for Jev's kinds and risk (`classify: true`) only while it is sorted
Riskiest first or grouped by kind; with neither picked nothing is asked (DESIGN.md
checklist 53; architecture, Jev).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;motion] home-pull-for-commands
Pulling the Inbox down past its top says "Pull for commands", then "Release for commands",
and letting go opens Commands with no refresh indicator. Tavi is "very in love with
that" (rules 52 and 117; F4).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design] home-pill-clears-the-gesture-bar
The bottom search pill sits clear of the system gesture bar and rides on top of the
keyboard when it is up (rules 47 and 55).
